{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And all the souls.</b> Meaning, with Joseph who was in Egypt they were seventy, and then there is no need to count Yocheved, who was born between the walls — in the name of Rabbi Shlomon ben Parḥon, of blessed memory. Therefore it counts them now, even though it counted them in their lifetime, because its intent was afterward: ״וירבו ויעצמו״ — to inform you that the seventy souls alone multiplied and grew until six hundred thousand footmen."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The bracketed [ששבעים] appears to be a gloss explaining that 'forty' is a scribal error for 'seventy'; translated as written."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:02:26.215691996Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}